Z||000010||MinnGreenGT||09-12-2001||11:34 AM||||I agree with all the above... got into the link, and it was still the pre-show info.  Where to go?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif">  <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000011||Archie||09-12-2001||11:53 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ChopTop:<BR><B>Couldn't find photos, or links to photos.  Possible you have to be a member.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>We, at NIFE, would like to encourage people to join our Club. The membership cost is not very much and you get 6 issues of our award winning Club newsletter that is published on time everytime. There are a lot of other good reasons to join NIFE. However NIFE doesn't restrict access to the web site to members only.<P>I swear that the pictures WERE on the NIFE web site when I started this thread. Something happened to the links to the FieroRama coverage. We've speculated that there may have been a server problem that caused the Web Site to be reloaded from back-up. As you know soon after I started this thread some of you had trouble loading the site. At this time it is speculated that the Host may have had a server problem and upon correction of the problem, they had to reload the site from their back-up copy. EMails have been sent to the Webmaster and I'm sure he will correct the problem by reloading the latest copy of the site.<P>So, as they say, "Please Stand By".<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000012||Dave Gunsul||09-12-2001||07:42 PM||||Right now the web-site is having problems<BR>but one thing I noticed was that Archie put the old address up. If you want to see the pictures of the attendies click on the events<BR>area on the left then scroll down the til you see the Fierorama on sept 9th and then click on the attendies photo line.<BR>The new address for the NIFE web-site is: <A HREF="http://www.fierofocus.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fierofocus.com</A> <P>Hmmm, I just went in there and the pics are missing from where they were the other day.<BR>Wonder what happened.<BR>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver<P>[This message has been edited by Dave Gunsul (edited 09-12-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Dave Gunsul (edited 09-12-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000013||Archie||09-12-2001||10:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Dave Gunsul:<BR><B><BR>Hmmm, I just went in there and the pics are missing from where they were the other day.<BR>Wonder what happened.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hmmmmmm, I guess that means you are saying I was right.<P>BTW, the FieroFocus address is correct but if you click on the link you provided it actually directs you to <A HREF="http://home.xnet.com/~nife/" TARGET=_blank>http://home.xnet.com/~nife/</A> <P>I just rec'd. and EMail that confirms the speculation I made earlier about a server problem was correct. I just rec'd. the following statement via EMail "They were loaded once Sunday night. Apparently there was a server crash, and our guess is that the ISP reloaded from backup tape early this am. (Wed) Our webmaster was contacted at 9PM today, he will upload the files again tonight. Check late tonight or Thursday AM."<P>Archie ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Dave Gunsul||09-12-2001||11:10 PM||||I just got the same email too.<P>I heard at one of the meetings that that old address won't be in use for much longer so I<BR>was just going by what I was told.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
